// Specialized NTC decode. Host side: cpp/include/ntc/fast.hpp.
// Generated by shaders/gen_ntc_fast.py. Edit the generator, not this file.
//
// Every shape, width, and parameter offset is a specialization constant.
// Private arrays are indexed only by literals, so after specialization every
// element is a register and no variant needs scratch memory. Layer outputs go
// to private arrays of at most 32 words (the row loop is the only dynamic
// index), or to workgroup memory with NTC_FAST_LDS. MLP parameters live in a
// uniform buffer at offsets known at pipeline creation: constant-bank
// operands on NVIDIA, scalar (SGPR) loads on AMD. Latents are channel planes whose record is a power of two of at most
// 32 bits, one aligned load per tap.
//
// Variants (pick one define before the include):
//   NTC_FAST_EXACT  NoContraction on every lerp and product. Bit-identical
//                   to ntc::decode_mip under default fp32 rounding.
//   (none)          fma for lerps and dots. Within 1e-5 of the reference.
//   NTC_FAST_FP16   packed fp16 weights and activations, f16vec2 fma
//                   (v_pk_fma_f16 on AMD, HFMA2 on NVIDIA), fp16 sums. fp32
//                   bias, scale and output. Needs shaderFloat16 only: no
//                   16-bit storage, weights are unpacked from 32-bit uniform
//                   words. 75 to 81 dB against fp32: the fp16 sum is the
//                   limit, not the fp16 activations.
//   NTC_FAST_I8     int8 weights times integer activation codes with
//                   dotPacked4x8EXT, exact int32 sums. act_int8 files use the
//                   file's scale and signed codes. Otherwise each layer input
//                   gets a max-abs scale: layer 0 has 16-bit codes (high and
//                   low byte, two dots), inputs after a ReLU unsigned 8-bit
//                   codes, others signed 8-bit. Grouped layers with
//                   group % 4 != 0 fall back to fp32.
//   NTC_FAST_I16    with NTC_FAST_I8: 16-bit codes on every layer. Two dots
//                   per 4 weights, the instruction count of packed fp16, with
//                   exact sums: over 100 dB against fp32.
//
// API: ntcf_eval(uv, mip) decodes one sample, then ntcf_y(c) is channel c
// for a literal c < NTCF_OUTCH.
//
// Bindings (set 0): 0 uniform params, 1 storage latents. The including
// shader owns every other binding and the push constants.

#ifdef NTC_FAST_FP16
#extension GL_EXT_shader_explicit_arithmetic_types_float16 : require
#endif
#ifdef NTC_FAST_I8
#extension GL_EXT_integer_dot_product : require
#endif

